theorem two-divided-equations-subtracted
  note        A − (p/q − r/s) is (A + B − p/q) − (B − r/s): the two cited equations taken by 1 and −1, each read with its own divisor.
  let A ∈ ℝ    (H1)
  let B ∈ ℝ    (H2)
  let p ∈ ℤ    (H3)
  let q ∈ ℕ    (H4)
  let r ∈ ℤ    (H5)
  let s ∈ ℕ    (H6)
  assume A + B = p/q    (H7)
  assume B = r/s    (H8)
  then A = p/q − r/s

1.  A = p/q − r/s
    algebra, from H7, H8
